   The (w/v) notation means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution.

2. **Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:**  
   Since the concentration is given as 0.044 grams per 100 mL, we can set up a proportion:  
   \[
   \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} = \frac{x \text{ g}}{10 \text{ mL}}
   \]  
   Solving for \( x \):  
   \[
   x = \frac{0.044 \text{ g} \times 10 \text{ mL}}{100 \text{ mL}} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
   \]

3. **Convert grams to milligrams:**  
   Since 1 gram = 1000 milligrams,  
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 = 4.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

