1. Increased temperatures: Higher temperatures can lead to an increase in the growth and survival of pathogens, which can lead to an increase in the prevalence of parasitic infections. This is particularly likely for pathogens that are temperature-dependent, such as the gut mites, the common host of the parasitic fungus ""E. coli*.

