","The type of carbon-containing product produced when Grignogen reagents react with carbon dioxide (CO₂) is a **ester**. The reaction proceeds in two steps:

### Step 1: Reaction with CO₂
The Grignion reagent (MCl₂) reacts with CO₂ to form a **carboxylate ion**.

\[
\text{MgCl}_2 + \text{CO}_2 \rightarrow \text{CO}_2\text{MgCl}_2
\]

### Step 2: Hydrorolysis
The carboxylate ion is then hydrolyzed (usually by dissolving the solution in water or adding an acid) to form the **ester**.

\[
\text{CO}_2\text{MgCl}_2 + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{CO}_2\text{HCl} + \text{MgOH}_2
\]

Thus, the overall reaction produces an **ester**. 

\[
\text{MgCl}_2 + \text{CO}_2 + \text{H}_2\text{O} \rightarrow \text{C}_2\text{H}_6\text{O}_3
\]

### Final Answer: $\boxed{\text{Ester}}$",relevance,"# Task Description
