","The vapor pressure of a substance is the pressure at which its liquid phase is in equilibrium with its vapor phase at a given temperature. A higher vapor pressure means the substance evaporates more readily, increasing the concentration of its vapor in the air.  

The PEL is the maximum safe concentration of a substance in the air that a person can be exposed to during a certain period of time.  

