1. **Identify the given proposition**:
   \[
   P \implies Q \implies \text{If } A \cup B = A \implies \text{Then } A \cap B = B.
   \]

2. **Negverse the conclusion**:
   \[
   Q^{-1} \implies \text{Not } A \cap B = B \implies A \cap B \neq B.
   \]

3. **Combine the original premise with the reversed conclusion**:
   \[
   P \wedge Q^{-1} \implies (A \cup B = A) \wedge (A \cap B \neq B).
   \]

