   \]

2. The limit of the oscillating term:
   \[
   \lim_{t \to \infty} \left[(1/3)\sin t + \cos t\right] e^{-t/2}.
   \]
   Since \( \sin t \) and \( \cos t \) oscillate between \(-1\) and \( 1 \), the term \( (1/3)\sin t + \cos t \) oscillates between \( -1/3 \) and \( 1 + 1/3 = 4/3 \).

   The term \( e^{-t/2} \) decays to 0 as \( t \to \infty \).

