"In an elastic scattering process where the electron mass is negligible, let the initial and final four-momenta of the electron be \( P_i = (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i) \) and \( P_f = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) \), respectively. Derive an expression for the squared four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \).","<bos><start_of_turn>user
In an elastic scattering process where the electron mass is negligible, let the initial and final four-momenta of the electron be \( P_i = (E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_i) \) and \( P_f = (E_f/c, \mathbf{p}_f) \), respectively. Derive an expression for the squared four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \).<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The square four-momentum transfer \( Q^2 \) is defined as the difference between the initial and final four-momenta:

\[
Q^2 = (P_f - P_i)^2
\]

Substituting the initial and final four-momenta:

\[
Q^2 = (P_f - P_i)^2 = (E_f/c - E_i/c, \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i)^2
\]

Expanding the square:

\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f}{c} - \frac{E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right) \cdot \left( \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \right)
\]

Expanding the cross product term:

\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_i - \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_f + \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i
\]

Since \( \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_i = \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_f \), the cross product terms cancel out:

\[
Q^2 = \left( \frac{E_f - E_i}{c} \right)^2 + \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f - \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i
\]

Using the definition of the square of the momentum:

\[
\mathbf{p} \cdot \mathbf{p} = p^2
\]

