     - \( T_s = 100° \text{°C} \) (surface temperature of the plate)  
     - \( T_\infty = 50° \text{°C} \) (free stream temperature of the air)  
     - \( V \) (free stream velocity of the air)  
     - \( A = 0.2 \, \text{m} \times 0.1 \, \text{m} = 0.02 \, \text{m}^2 \) (surface area of the plate)  

2. **Calculate the free stream velocity \( V \):**  
   - The Reynolds number \( Re \) is given by:  
     \[
     Re = \frac{\rho \cdot V \cdot L}{\mu}
     \]  
     where:  
     - \( L = 0.2 \, \text{m} \) (length of the plate)  
     - \( \mu = 0.0021 \, \text{Pa·s} \) (dynamic viscosity of air at 50°C)  
   - Solving for \( V \):  
     \[
     V = \frac{Re \cdot \mu}{0.2 \cdot \rho} = \frac{40,000 \cdot 0.0021}{0.2 \cdot 1.2} = 3.5 \, \text{m/s}
     \]  

