   \[ 2 \text{H}_2(g) + \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{H}_2\text{O}(l) \]

2. **Calculate the standard Gibbs free energy change for the reaction (\(\Delta G^\circ\)):**
   The standard Gibbs free energy change for a reaction is calculated using the standard Gibbs free energy of formation (\(\Delta G^\circ_f\)) of the products and products:
   \[
   \Delta G^\circ = \sum_i n_i \Delta G^\circ_f(i) \text{ (products)} - \sum_i n_i \Delta G^\circ_f(i) \text{ (reactants)}
   \]
   For the reaction above:
   \[
   \Delta G^\circ = 2 \times \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{H}_2\text{O}(l)) - 2 \times \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{H}_2(g)) - 1 \times \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{O}_2(g))
   \]
