   \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{H}_2\text{O}(l)) = -237.1 \text{ kJ/mol}
   \]
   The standard Gibbs free energy of formation for hydrogen and oxygen is zero:
   \[
   \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{H}_2(g)) = 0 \text{ kJ/mol}
   \]
   \[
   \Delta G^\circ_f(\text{O}_2(g)) = 0 \text{ kJ/mol}
   \]
   Substituting these values:
   \[
   \Delta G^\circ = 2 \times (-237.1) - 2 \times 0 - 1 \times 0 = -474.2 \text{ kJ}
   \]

3. **Calculate the change in Gibbs free energy for the given amounts:**
